  "summary": "The identified studies apply transformer-based architectures, specifically Self-Attention Encoder Models, to the task of electricity consumption forecasting. Haddad et al. [V0126] and Gupta et al. [V0125] report strong predictive performance with MAE of 0.93 and accuracy of 0.86, respectively. Additional investigations by Adebayo et al. [V0127] and Brennan et al. [V0128] further demonstrate the application of these models across different datasets. A comparative study by Brennan et al. [V0131] also addresses electricity consumption prediction but employs Decentralised Training Without Pooled Records.",
